1
00:00:00,797 --> 00:00:02,997
(Dr Hofstadter:)It's fascinating.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,570
(Dr Hofstadter:)How can someone
as enlightened as Sheldon

3
00:00:05,569 --> 00:00:08,739
(Dr Hofstadter:)come from someone like you?

4
00:00:08,739 --> 00:00:10,309
(Mrs Cooper:)I know the answer.

5
00:00:10,307 --> 00:00:11,577
(Mrs Cooper:)You're not gonna like it.

6
00:00:11,575 --> 00:00:13,905
(Dr Hofstadter:)Try me.

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:16,411
(Mrs Cooper:)When I was pregnant with Shelly,
I was driving to church,

8
00:00:16,413 --> 00:00:17,713
(Mrs Cooper:)and I was praying
to the Lord

9
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:21,885
(Mrs Cooper:)to give me a son smarter
than his dumb-ass daddy.

10
00:00:22,885 --> 00:00:26,155
(Mrs Cooper:)And I looked over
and I saw a Jesus bobblehead

11
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:29,496
(Mrs Cooper:)in the Subaru next to me
nodding yes.

12
00:00:36,532 --> 00:00:38,232
(Mrs Cooper:)What is that supposed to mean?

13
00:00:38,235 --> 00:00:42,435
It means... I can't believe
we're having this conversation.

14
00:00:42,439 --> 00:00:43,609
(Mrs Cooper:)Well, do it some more.

15
00:00:43,607 --> 00:00:46,907
(Mrs Cooper:)Maybe you can knock
some sense into yourself.

16
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:49,280
Why don't we all stops
hitting ourselves

17
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:50,949
(Penny:)and talk about something
safe, you know,

18
00:00:50,948 --> 00:00:55,348
(Penny:)like shoes or how cute
little Chinese babies are.

19
00:00:55,352 --> 00:00:56,852
(Sheldon:)It is not my fault
that your mother likes me

20
00:00:56,854 --> 00:00:58,724
better than she likes you!
Oh, don't flatter yourself!

